-- src/eval/journal/admission.ail
--
-- ADR-004 v5 D2 "The entry", "Framing", "The program" and D3 A5, A6, A9, A9b;
-- PLAN-004 §3 P1.6: the admission run, the program, provenance. The pure half:
--
--   admission_program(jw, w0, log, m, gv)   -> ExecutionProgram
--   preflight(kind, ids, cmp)               -> [AdmissionFinding]   (A9 manifest shape, A9b)
--   check_a5(frame) / check_a6(end, n, obs) / check_a9(program)
--   decode_identities / decode_comparators  (the shell's gathered files)
--
-- The run itself — `admission_run`, the observations taken from a
-- `TracedSessionResult`, and `admit` — is `admission_run.ail`. The split is
-- forced: in a module that imports `src/core/session`, `std/json`'s
-- `getString`/`getBool` demand SharedMem under `ailang test` (AILANG v0.33.0,
-- reproduced on a two-line probe), so this module, whose tests decode JSON,
-- does not import it.
--
-- THE RUN. `run_v2_session_traced` (session.ail:4423) with the recorded
-- `BootInputs` (task, env_url, hybrid_tools, budget, ohmy_pi, cost rates), the
-- LOGICAL model, the seed, a throwaway `workdir`, `step_budget = N`,
-- `max_cost_millicents: 0`, an `ExtRuntime` with an EMPTY registry and
-- `verification.enabled = false`, and `PortedWorld(journal_ports(rt), w0)`
-- (`seams.journal_provider`, P1.5). The caller frames it: `WORLD_RUN_BEGIN
-- <label> <ordinal0>` before, `WORLD_RUN_END <label> <final>` after, and
-- `WORLD_RUN_REFUSED <label> pending=<n>` instead of END when the returned
-- world still holds witnesses (`ledger_parity_dst.ail:436–452`'s rule).
--
-- THE PROGRAM. Schema `program_schema_version()` (execution-program/4),
-- `generator_id: "journal_admission"`, the generator version the runner
-- gathered, seed 0, `initial_world` as D2 (messages_and_policy: canonical JSON
-- of session, selector, seed digest, seed count, expected end, T0 settings;
-- the world's env, the synthetic profile file, the declared epoch,
-- `driver_only/<version>`), OBSERVED bounds as data (`chunk_draw_hi` 0; not a
-- limit — `validate_program` does not call `validate_bounds`), the manifest
-- `driver_only_manifest` builds from the gathered values, and
-- `interactions = world.log`.
--
-- THE CHECKS LANDED HERE (P1.7a/P1.7b land A1–A4, A7, A8 and the verdict):
--   A5  framing: the markers re-parsed (a malformed or mislabelled marker is a
--       finding), >= 1 `world_request` in the frame, ordinals strictly
--       ordinal0+1, ordinal0+2, … (from the trace's `WorldRequest` records),
--       last == final, empty pending queue. Location `Aggregate("frame")`.
--   A6  end: EndSuspended(N) = `result` Err code `StepBudgetExhausted`,
--       `suspended: Some`, exactly one `RunSuspended` in the trace, N provider
--       records; EndFinalize(model_stop) = `result` Ok, `suspended: None`, no
--       `RunSuspended`, the `RunSummary` finish reason `stop`, N provider
--       records. Then, independently, NO EXHAUSTED MARKER anywhere in the log
--       (an explicit scan for `encode_exhausted_provider_outcome()`'s payload
--       on provider records). Locations `Call(k)`, 1-based: the end mismatch at
--       the observed provider-record count, a marker at its record's seq + 1.
--   A9  round trip, in the ADR's order: `validate_program`,
--       `validate_manifest(m, driver_only())`, `world_state_of`,
--       `reconstitution_balance` against the world `world_state_of` built. A
--       rejection naming an ordinal is at `Interaction(ordinal)`; a manifest,
--       schema or balance finding at `Aggregate(...)`.
--   A9b provenance: each gathered identity against the comparator PLAN-004
--       §3 P1.6's table names, below. Before the run (here, `preflight`) and
--       after it (the shell re-collects and re-runs the check; a changed
--       identity between the two collections is its own finding there).
--
-- A9b's COMPARATORS, narrowed exactly as the table says:
--   source_revision   the rev is a commit (`git cat-file -e <rev>^{commit}`),
--                     no tracked change outside the corpus, and the assembled
--                     tree's hash (computed from the files, not from git
--                     status) equals `<rev>^{tree}`
--   scan_root_commit  the same revision (both are A)
--   toolchain         the binary SHA-256 and version pinned in E's record.
--                     No record before P1G: a REAL entry is refused
--                     (`ToolchainUnpinned`); a synthetic one is not, and the
--                     report says the toolchain was not checked.
--   abi_version       the `sunholo/motoko_ext_abi` version in `ailang.lock`
--   classifier_2_set, unrouted_fields
--                     NOT a second extractor: the reviewed pinned record, the
--                     literals in `scripts/dst/profile_definition_dst.ail`
--   scan_roots        the profile's `scan_roots` (`driver_only()`), root for
--                     root, and every driver leaf (`SCAN_FILES`) inside them
--   packages / lock   E's pinned package inputs (name, source, version,
--                     interface hash — never the path) and lock SHA-256;
--                     unpinned: a REAL entry is refused
--   normalized_configuration
--                     `gen_fixtures.py`'s config reader, re-derived
--   profile/rule/vocabulary versions
--                     CONSISTENCY ONLY with the same `driver_only_manifest`
--                     builder `validate_manifest` compares against
--   generator_version E's pinned commit; a `-dev` generator refuses a REAL
--                     entry (before P1G it is always `-dev`)
--   extension_packages the registry the run used: empty
-- A BLANK gathered string (or an empty required list) is not A9b's finding:
-- presence is `validate_manifest`'s, reported first as A9 on the manifest the
-- preflight builds. `unrouted_fields` may legitimately be empty and is always
-- compared. None of `validate_manifest`, `driver_only_manifest`'s caller
-- inputs or `strict_replay_dst.ail:631–633`'s fixture literals is used as a
-- truth source.
--
-- Privacy (§0.6): synthetic fixtures only; findings carry identities, counts,
-- ordinals and digests.

